b. Best interests of the child;
c. Right to life, survival and development;
d. Respect for the views of the child;
- 7 -
e. Gender equality;
f. Gender justice;
g. Legal certainty

Article 5
In order to realize the objectives as referred to in Article 3 letter b, efforts shall be made through:
a. establishment, development, and capacity strengthening of institutions for the protection of women and children including complaint service units for violence against women and children, as well as legal aid services;
b. improvement of the quality of human resources management;
c. institutional capacity strengthening of Gender Mainstreaming (PUG) and children;
d. strengthening and development of gender and children data systems.

REGENT OF SAMPANG
PROVINCE OF EAST JAVA
REGIONAL REGULATION OF SAMPANG REGENCY NUMBER 7 OF 2017
CONCERNING
WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION
BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY
REGENT OF SAMPANG,

Considering : a. that every citizen has equal rights to live a dignified life in accordance with the principles of humanity, equality, and justice;
b. that women's empowerment is carried out so that women can actualize their potential optimally to participate in development in accordance with their capacity;
c. that women who constitute a vulnerable group need to receive special protection so that they do not experience violence and can live a decent life in accordance with the principles of humanity, equality and justice;
d. that with the enactment of Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 Concerning the System of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection, the regional government needs to improve the quality of life of women and protect children.
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

